        Secret Management at Scale: Injecting 1Password / Vault Secrets Directly into `act`
      </h2>
      <p>
        For enterprise engineering teams adhering to strict security compliance regimes, storing plaintext <code>.secrets</code> files on developer laptops—even with <code>.gitignore</code> rules—violates corporate security guidelines.
      </p>
      <p>
        Instead, stream credentials dynamically into <code>act</code> directly from encrypted enterprise secret managers (such as 1Password CLI or HashiCorp Vault) without ever persisting plaintext files to the physical disk:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto"><code># Method A: Inject secrets dynamically via 1Password CLI (op run)
op run --env-file=.secrets.tpl -- act -j test -P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest

# Method B: Stream secrets directly from HashiCorp Vault via bash process substitution
act -j integration-tests \
  --secret-file &lt;(vault kv get -format=json secret/ci/testing | jq -r '.data.data | to_entries[] | "\(.key)=\(.value)"') \
  -s GITHUB_TOKEN=&#36;(gh auth token) \
  -P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
</code></pre>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Automated Local Verification Script with Pre-Flight Docker Health Diagnostics
      </h2>
      <p>
        The shell script below wraps <code>nektos/act</code> in defensive pre-flight health checks. It verifies that the Docker daemon is responding, checks for runner image caching, ensures <code>.secrets</code> is excluded from git tracking, and acquires an authenticated GitHub token automatically:
      </p>

      <pre is:raw class="bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>#!/usr/bin/env bash
# run-act-safe.sh: Defensive wrapper for local GitHub Actions debugging
set -euo pipefail

log() {
  echo "[$(date -u +'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')] [INFO] $1"
}

log_error() {
  echo "[$(date -u +'%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')] [ERROR] $1" >&2
}

# 1. Verify Docker Daemon
log "Checking Docker daemon connectivity..."
if ! docker info >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  log_error "Docker is not running! Please start Docker Desktop, OrbStack, or Colima."
  exit 1
fi

# 2. Verify .secrets quarantine
if [ -f .secrets ]; then
  if ! git check-ignore -q .secrets; then
    log_error "CRITICAL: .secrets exists but is NOT ignored by git! Aborting."
    exit 1
  fi
  SECRET_ARG="--secret-file .secrets"
else
  log "No .secrets file found; running in zero-secrets mode."
  SECRET_ARG=""
fi

# 3. Acquire GitHub Auth Token
GH_TOKEN=""
if command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  GH_TOKEN=&#36;(gh auth token 2>/dev/null || true)
fi

TOKEN_ARG=""
if [ -n "$GH_TOKEN" ]; then
  TOKEN_ARG="-s GITHUB_TOKEN=$GH_TOKEN"
  log "Injected authenticated GitHub CLI token."
fi

# 4. Dispatch act execution
JOB_NAME=&#36;{1:-""}
RUNNER_IMAGE="catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest"

if [ -n "$JOB_NAME" ]; then
  log "Executing specific job: $JOB_NAME"
  act -j "$JOB_NAME" $SECRET_ARG $TOKEN_ARG -P ubuntu-latest="$RUNNER_IMAGE"
else
  log "Executing all push workflow jobs..."
  act push $SECRET_ARG $TOKEN_ARG -P ubuntu-latest="$RUNNER_IMAGE"
fi
</code></pre>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
