      <ul class="space-y-4 text-slate-300">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">1. Error: "Could not find image" or Silent Image Pull Hangs:</strong> By default, act pulls from Docker Hub. If rate-limited or offline, the job terminates. <em>Remediation:</em> Pre-pull the image manually via <code>docker pull catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest</code> and specify <code>--pull=false</code> to enforce local caching.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">2. Error: "Cannot connect to the Docker daemon":</strong> On macOS or Windows WSL2, the Docker socket path may not match <code>/var/run/docker.sock</code>. <em>Remediation:</em> Export <code>DOCKER_HOST="unix://$HOME/.docker/run/docker.sock"</code> or specify <code>--container-daemon-socket</code> explicitly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">3. Composite Actions Failing with "Private Repo 404":</strong> If your workflow references custom shared actions in private GitHub repositories (e.g. <code>uses: my-org/shared-action@v2</code>), act cannot clone them without authorization. <em>Remediation:</em> Pass an authenticated token via <code>-s GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">4. Localhost Network Access Refused:</strong> If a job step attempts to connect to a local database running on your host machine via <code>localhost:5432</code>, it fails because <code>localhost</code> inside Docker refers to the container itself. <em>Remediation:</em> Point connection strings to <code>host.docker.internal:5432</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">5. File Permission &amp; UID Discrepancies:</strong> Docker steps running as <code>root</code> inside the container may write artifacts to your working directory that are uneditable by your host user. <em>Remediation:</em> Pass <code>--userns=host</code> or configure your step with <code>chmod -R 777 .</code> in an <code>always()</code> post-run step.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Frequently Asked Questions: Running nektos/act Locally with Sensitive Credentials
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">What is nektos/act and how does it run GitHub Actions locally?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            nektos/act is an open-source Go CLI tool that reads your local .github/workflows/*.yml files, parses the job steps, and executes them inside isolated Docker containers mirroring GitHub-hosted runner environments.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How do you pass secrets to act without hardcoding them?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Use the '--secret-file' flag pointing to a local .secrets key-value file: 'act --secret-file .secrets'. Ensure .secrets is strictly added to .gitignore and git global excludes to prevent accidental repository commits.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How do you mock secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN in local act runs?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Provide a personal access token (PAT) inside .secrets as GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxx, or pass it inline via '-s GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)' to enable API actions and package downloads.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-4 bg-slate-900/40">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-2">How can I prevent committing .secrets to version control?</h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Add '.secrets' to both your repository's .gitignore and your local .git/info/exclude, and configure a git pre-commit hook that aborts any commit attempting to stage filenames matching .secrets*.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

